  "port_policy": "Preserve source algorithms; changes are explicit infrastructure adapters or regression-tested bug fixes.",
  "official_base_commit": "2c43c5890357dae71096132ea3ade7cfa32d734c",
  "port_notes": [
    "Package-qualified imports replace project sys.path assumptions.",
    "Reporting resource and output paths are explicit configuration.",
    "Final-transcript segment-aware GFF flush is covered by a regression test.",
    "Oncofusion aggregation preserves original uid__library grouping; raw scans preserve physical source IDs.",
    "Empty oncofusion gene-pair tables retain their schema.",
    "PTD callable adapter is checked against saved v2/v3 read identities and evidence; ITD cluster membership is checked against all archived groups.",
    "Deep sequence-validation utilities retain their original gates; discovery does not imply that these utilities assessed every event.",
    "Official barcode recognizer now accepts an existing numeric lane suffix, so reverse=TRUE is applied to standard 10x BAM barcodes; raw counts and bulk identities remain unchanged. Standard regression baseline uses a separately recorded identical one-line compatibility fix.",
    "Raw annotation writer is explicitly closed before compression; regression cases reproduce and prevent loss of buffered rows, preserving complete raw/native source rosters. Standard comparison records this identical one-line I/O fix in the preserved official baseline."
  ]
}
